{"text": "Ramcharan Petit Family Law Professional Corporation\nNOTES TO FILE - financial disclosure, Form 13.1 - PRIVILEGED\n\nFile: Desrochers / Banh - our no. 26-0417-SR - Court file FC-26-1184 (Superior Court\nof Justice, Family Branch, Ottawa)\n\nMeeting Thurs. 21 May 2026, Mireille Desrochers with Sunita Ramcharan (SR).\nOpposing counsel: Gordon Wojcik, Wojcik & Oyelade LLP, 613-555-0171,\ngwojcik@wojcikoyelade.example.\n\nParties and children\nMireille, born 4 Feb 1986, SIN 359-185-956. Husband Thanh Kelvin Banh, goes by\nKelvin, born 1983-11-30, SIN 527 469 837 (from the 2024 joint mortgage renewal,\nhe has not produced it). Married 16 Aug 2012 in Gatineau; separated Jan 3/26 (he\nsays Feb. 14, when he moved to his brother's in Orléans). V-day will be argued.\n\n Élodie Banh, born 09/06/2014, Grade 6 at École élémentaire Sainte-Geneviève.\nCompetitive swimming, $3,180 a year.\n Marc-Antoine Banh (\"Marco\"), born 22 March 2017. ADHD, combined type, on\nBiphentin 20 mg; IEP at the same school; OT at $140 a session, not covered.\nÉlodie and Marco are with Mireille 10 nights of 14 since January.\n\nIncome (Part 2)\nMireille: dental hygienist, Byward Smiles Dental Hygiene, 4 days a week. 2025 T4\nbox 14 $71,460.12; CRA Notice of Assessment line 15000 $73,902. Kelvin: optical\nengineer, Kanata Photonics Inc., employee no. KP-20418, base $148,500 plus bonus\n(2025: 38,250). He also has RSUs he calls \"worthless\"; SR to demand the grant\nstatements.\n\nAssets and debts on V-day (Part 4)\n Matrimonial home, 62 Wigan Drive, Nepean, ON K2J 3T8. Joint. Appraised\n$912,000 by Tavish Imrie of Imrie Appraisals Ltd., report IA-26-0338. Mortgage\nwith Dominion Lakehead Bank, no. 4410-778-203961, balance $388,214.67;\nHELOC $41,900.\n Joint chequing, Kawartha Shores Credit Union, transit 04512, institution 842,\naccount 6017733: $6,244.10.\n\n Her savings at Kawartha Shores, acct ending -2290: $18,700. Gift from her\nmother Huguette Desrochers ($15,000, Dec. 2024) - excluded property if we can\ntrace it. Huguette will swear an affidavit.\n His RRSP at Dominion Lakehead, plan RSP 77-1204-5: $203,118. Her RRSP\n$54,300; TFSA $11,025.40. RESP for both kids, $46,880, joint subscribers.\n 2021 Honda CR-V, plate CKRT 482, VIN 2HKRW2H84MH614273, hers, worth\nabout $27,500. 2016 Mazda3, plate BXMJ917, his, $9,000.\n Debts: joint Visa ending 7042 ($4,812.33, both are cardholders); Kelvin's\nMastercard 5532 6879 7315 9320 - Mireille found the statement, $22,406.90,\nmostly online sports betting, he denies it. Loan from his brother, \"twenty\nthousand\", undocumented.\n\nSupport\nTable child support on his 2025 income approx. $2,610/mo; s. 7 expenses shared\n28/72. He has paid $1,500 by e-transfer twice (Feb 27 and April 1) to\nmireille.desrochers@courriel.example. Spousal: mid-range about $1,150 monthly,\n5-10 yrs. If he stops paying we register with FRO.\n\nTo do\n SR: serve Form 13.1 and Request for Information by June 12, 2026; case\nconference 2026-07-08.\n Mireille: 3 years of Notices of Assessment, Kawartha statements, pension\nstatement (HOOPP member no. 0048-221-907). She can be reached on (613)\n555-0138 after 4, not at work.\n Do not email her at the shared family address; Kelvin still has the tablet.", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 492 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Ramcharan Petit", "Mireille Desrochers", "Thanh Kelvin Banh", "Élodie Banh", "Marc-Antoine Banh", "Gordon Wojcik", "Tavish Imrie", "Huguette Desrochers", "Kelvin", "Mireille desrochers"], "companies": ["Ramcharan Petit Family Law Professional Corporation", "Desrochers", "Banh", "Sunita Ramcharan", "Wojcik & Oyelade LLP", "Kanata Photonics Inc.", "Dominion Lakehead Bank", "Kawartha Shores Credit Union", "Imrie Appraisals Ltd.", "Byward Smiles Dental Hygiene", "Kelvin", "Kawartha Shores", "Dominion Lakehead", "Visa", "Mastercard", "HOOPP"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 76.59999999776483, "modelMs": 44677.199999999255, "detectors": 